    <bpmn:process id="W_W3407" name="W3407. Market Outlook, Forecast &amp; Commodity Intelligence Briefing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly/monthly cadence; market shock event
Frequency: Weekly flash + monthly briefing
Volume: ~10–15 tracked commodities
Owner: Procurement Director
Participants: Procurement, Treasury, Category Managers (links to VS-01), Merchandising (links to VS-101), FP&amp;A
Source: workflow W3407 — Market Outlook, Forecast &amp; Commodity Intelligence Briefing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3407_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3407_Lane1" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3407_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3407_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3407_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3407_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3407_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3407_Start3" name="Weekly/monthly cadence; market shock event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3407_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3407_Task4" name="Procurement/Treasury compile the weekly commodity flash: price movement on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Procurement/Treasury compile the weekly commodity flash: price movement on tracked commodities/indices (W3403), key drivers (supply, demand, geopolitics, FX links to VS-18.3), BuildRight exposure impact (W3404), and any vendor/market signal (e.g., cement allocation, steel quota, shipping freight)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Treasury
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Weekly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3407_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3407_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3407_Task5" name="Procurement/Category Managers publish the monthly commodity intelligence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Procurement/Category Managers publish the monthly commodity intelligence briefing: outlook/forecast per commodity, scenario views, recommended buying/timing/hedging posture, and implications for OTB/receipts (links to VS-101 W3283/W3284) and pricing (links to VS-01.2/W3417); brief Merchandising and FP&amp;A
Responsible (R): Procurement / Category Managers
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3407_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3407_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3407_Task6" name="Procurement/Treasury convene ad-hoc briefings on market shocks (oil spike…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Procurement/Treasury convene ad-hoc briefings on market shocks (oil spike, steel quota, typhoon supply disruption links to VS-69) and trigger the rapid-response mitigation (links to PA-106.2/W3418) and price-action (links to VS-01.2/W329) workflow; document decisions for governance (W3406)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Treasury / Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3407_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3407_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3407_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3407_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-547 (ensure controlled execution — Commodity Exposure Identification &amp; Market Intelligence (PA-106.1).) | - operational: scenario ranges and humility bias; operational: weekly flash and event triggers
Owner: Procurement Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
