    <bpmn:process id="W_W3408" name="W3408. Import-FX-Commodity Interaction &amp; Landed-Cost Exposure Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import buy planning (links to VS-02.2); monthly exposure review
Frequency: Monthly + import-cycle
Volume: ~40% of COGS import; ~400–600 TEUs/month (per profile §7.1)
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Manager, Import/Procurement (links to VS-02.2/VS-87), FP&amp;A, Logistics Finance (links to VS-17)
Source: workflow W3408 — Import-FX-Commodity Interaction &amp; Landed-Cost Exposure Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3408_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3408_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3408_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3408_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3408_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3408_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3408_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3408_Start3" name="Import buy planning (links to VS-02.2); monthly exposure review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3408_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3408_Task4" name="Treasury/Import decompose the import landed cost into commodity + FX +…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Treasury/Import decompose the import landed cost into commodity + FX + freight/duty + handling components (links to VS-02.2 W2B.12 landed cost, VS-87 duty, VS-18.3 FX), and quantify each component&#x27;s share and volatility for top import commodities (steel, copper, tiles, paint raws, tools)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Import
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3408_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3408_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3408_Task5" name="Treasury measure the interaction/correlation between commodity price, FX…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Treasury measure the interaction/correlation between commodity price, FX (PHP/USD, PHP/CNY), and freight (per VS-06/VS-87), and the combined landed-cost sensitivity (e.g., steel up 10% + PHP weakens 5% + freight up 20%); isolate hedgeable vs unhedgeable components
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3408_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3408_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3408_Task6" name="Treasury/Import publish the integrated landed-cost exposure view, coordinate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Treasury/Import publish the integrated landed-cost exposure view, coordinate the FX hedge (links to VS-18.3/W80/W321) with the commodity hedge (PA-106.2), and feed the combined exposure to margin/price decisions (links to VS-101.3/VS-01.2) and the merchandise plan (links to VS-101)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Import / Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3408_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3408_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3408_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3408_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-547 (ensure controlled execution — Commodity Exposure Identification &amp; Market Intelligence (PA-106.1).) | - operational: integrated landed-cost analysis; operational: landed-cost decomposition
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3408_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3408_Annotation8" targetRef="W3408_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3408_Flow10" sourceRef="W3408_Start3" targetRef="W3408_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3408_Flow11" sourceRef="W3408_Task4" targetRef="W3408_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3408_Flow12" sourceRef="W3408_Task5" targetRef="W3408_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3408_Flow13" sourceRef="W3408_Task6" targetRef="W3408_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
